Hi Vincent,

We want to use GGIR to validate the %MVPA calculated in ActiLife. We know that ActiLife calculates the sum of activity counts on the Y axis to measure the activity intensity. Hence, in order to reproduce the ActiLife output in GGIR, I included the following arguments in the GGIR function:
do.enmo = F, do.neishabouricounts = T,
bout.metric = 1,
part5_agg2_60seconds = T,
threshold.lig = c(100),
threshold.mod = c(1952),
threshold.vig = c(5724),
actilife_LFE = T,
acc.metric = "NeishabouriCount_y",
HASIB.algo = "Sadeh1994",
Sadeh_axis = "Y"
However, the outputs produced from GGIR package has much lower percentages for moderate and vigorous activity and higher percentage for inactive and light activity time.
I am not sure about the reason why they have such different outputs but I am wondering if there could be a way to validate the output from ActiLife using GGIR package?
Any suggestions would be appreciated.

Best,
Jasmine

